specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:290:- It is invoked after the `connected` frame is sent, not before ([validated by: runs after the connected frame is sent, not before it](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L66)).
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:291:- It is not invoked inline in the `connection` listener, where a synchronous throw corrupts an already-upgraded socket. It runs on a microtask, which drains before the loop delivers any inbound frame ([validated by: is deferred, so it never runs inside the connection listener](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L77)).
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:292:- Both hooks widen to `void | Promise<void>` and are fire-and-forget. The engine never awaits either, and a hook that rejects does not reach the process ([validated by: survives a hook that rejects](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L98)).
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:293:- Both route through one helper that logs `{sessionId, error}` and swallows, so a throwing `onConnect` leaves the connection intact ([validated by: survives a hook that throws synchronously](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L86)).
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:294:- The same helper covers the close path, where a throwing `onDisconnect` would otherwise escape the `close` listener ([validated by: does not let a throwing hook escape the close listener](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L128)).
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/spec.md:295:- Either hook may be absent, and a connection without one behaves identically ([validated by: is optional, so a connection without one still sends its frame](../../src/transport/ws/connectionHandler.test.ts#L106)).
